      "title": "MOSS SFT PHOTOGRAPHY — START HERE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MOSS SFT photography\nEdit the photograph description, then Run. Your prompt goes directly to the model; prompt enhancement is off.\n\nSFT BF16 diffusion weights, full FLUX.2 VAE, 1216 × 1664 portrait, 25 steps, CFG 2.5, er_sde/simple. Full weights and a larger image need more memory. Image quality varies with the prompt and seed.\n\nDestripe targets color banding. Strength 1.5 follows the adapter author's 1024 px guidance; it is a starting point at this larger resolution. The second slot starts at 0 (off). Add only MOSS SFT-compatible diffusion LoRAs and follow their strength and trigger guidance.\n\nYour photographs save to output/moss/photography/.\n\nModel: https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-Image\nAdapter: https://huggingface.co/nynxz/MOSS-Image"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MOSS SFT photography\nEdit the photograph description, then Run. Your prompt goes directly to the model; prompt enhancement is off.\n\nSFT BF16 diffusion weights, full FLUX.2 VAE, 1216 × 1664 portrait, 25 steps, CFG 2.5, er_sde/simple. Full weights and a larger image need more memory. Image quality varies with the prompt and seed.\n\nDestripe targets color banding. Strength 1.5 follows the adapter author's 1024 px guidance; it is a starting point at this larger resolution. The second slot starts at 0 (off). Add only MOSS SFT-compatible diffusion LoRAs and follow their strength and trigger guidance.\n\nYour photographs save to output/moss/photography/.\n\nModel: https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-Image\nAdapter: https://huggingface.co/nynxz/MOSS-Image"
      },
      "color": "#254438",
      "bgcolor": "#232936"
    },
